{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.interacts_without_linking_of_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.interacts_without_linking_of_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L110-L116","doc":"The contrapositive, as the requirement on any future nucleus→link\nassignment: a triple carrying a nonzero well-defined `μ̄` must have a pair that\n**interacts without linking** — precisely what Brunnian means, and precisely what\n`interacts_iff_adj` forbids here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.mubarZero_of_milnorDefined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.mubarZero_of_milnorDefined","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L103-L108","doc":"**Definedness implies vanishing.** So no non-trivial well-defined Milnor\ntriple invariant exists in this closure, at any `A`: where `μ̄` is meaningful it\nis zero, and where it is nonzero it is not well defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.split_of_milnorDefined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.split_of_milnorDefined","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L94-L101","doc":"**The collapse: every Milnor-defined triple is split.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.not_linked_iff_not_interacts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.not_linked_iff_not_interacts","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L87-L92","doc":"**On a path, \"unlinked\" and \"non-interacting\" are the same condition.** This\nis the step that has no analogue for a Brunnian link, where components interact\nwhile their linking numbers vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.MilnorDefined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.MilnorDefined","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L82-L85","doc":"`μ̄(ijk)` is a genuine integer — `Δ = 0` — exactly when all three pairs are\nunlinked. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.mubar_zero_of_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.mubar_zero_of_split","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Classical: a split link has vanishing Milnor invariants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.split_of_not_interacts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.split_of_not_interacts","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Measured: three pairwise non-interacting components occupy pairwise\ndisjoint contiguous strand blocks, so the sublink is split. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.interacts_iff_adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.interacts_iff_adj","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Measured: exactly the adjacent pairs share a crossing — the closure has\n*zero* crossings between non-adjacent components, not merely a zero signed\nsum. This is what makes the collapse happen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.linked_iff_adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.linked_iff_adj","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Measured: exactly the adjacent pairs link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.MubarZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.MubarZero","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Milnor's `μ̄` vanishes on the triple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.Split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.Split","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The triple bounds a splitting into three pieces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.Interacts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.Interacts","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Some letter of the word acts on both components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.Linked","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.Linked","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The pair has nonzero linking number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.Adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.Adj","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Adjacency of the path `P_μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorPathCollapse.PathLinkingStructure","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorDefinedTriplesVanish.lean#L48-L78","doc":"The measured structure of the atom closure's linking, as a bundle of\nhypotheses. `Adj` is adjacency on the path; `Linked` records which pairs have\nnonzero linking number; `Interacts` records which pairs share a crossing; `Split`\nrecords which triples bound a splitting; `MubarZero` records the classical fact\nthat a split triple has vanishing Milnor invariant.\n\nThe class carries the *inputs* and the theorems below *derive* the conclusion —\n`Δ = 0 → μ̄ = 0` is not a field. ","signatureChunk":0}]}